This is done and committed as ed1c533a (Part of #1041). If a stdio MCP server dies mid-session, its tools are now dropped at the next turn, so the model stops calling a server that isn't there. fmt, clippy (-D warnings) and the full cargo test run all pass.

What changed
• One connect path. src/mcp_prefix.rs now has connect_mcp, built on a new mcp_tool_source(cmd, args, env, prefix: Option<&str>). It connects an McpClient, lists its tools once, and installs yoagent's McpToolSource (adding .with_prefix(p) only when there's a collision). Both config paths (--mcp and [mcp_servers.*]) and both cases (colliding or not) go through it. with_mcp_server_stdio and the hand-written list-once PrefixedMcpTools are gone. That listing at connect time means a server that can't list its tools still fails to connect, and its tool names are still recorded for the next server's collision check.
• Earlier servers survive a later failure. The new path never consumes the agent, so both MCP error arms lose their build_agent() rebuild, counter reset and "connections lost" note. If one MCP server fails, the ones before it stay connected. record_failed_server still runs, so the model still gets told. An OpenAPI failure still rebuilds the agent and still drops every MCP server.
• Guard counts updated, with the reason in each doc comment.
  • every_rebuild_arm_resets_the_counter_it_invalidated goes from 3/3/1/4 to 1/1/1/2, and now also checks that mcp_prefix.rs has no rebuild and no "connections lost" note.
  • The two every_connect_failure_arm_* guards also failed under the new code (the task didn't mention them). The MCP failure line moved into connect_mcp, so they now check that function's body too, with counts updated to match.
• src/agent_builder.rs shrank from 4955 to 4911 lines, within its size cap.
• One visible change: for a plain --mcp server, the success line now shows the whole sanitized command, not just its first word.

Tests: these live inside mcp_prefix.rs, not in a new tests/ file, because yoyo has no library target that an integration test could reach. A small sh script in a temp directory acts as a fake MCP server.
• a_server_that_exits_has_its_tools_withdrawn: kills the fake server and checks its tool disappears.
• a_live_server_keeps_its_tools_across_asks: the near-miss case, where a live server keeps its tool across two asks; it also checks the fs__ prefix.
• Positive control: I swapped in a list-once source as one mutate-run-restore command with a NEUTERED marker. Only the withdrawal test went red, and the code is restored.

Docs: I marked the old claims as superseded in place in CLAUDE.md and src/mcp_prefix.rs, and added the history under ARCHITECTURE.md's entry for mcp_prefix.rs, using the yoagent-version-claim: 0.25 marker. CLAUDE.md grew by about 500 bytes, to roughly 42 KB. It was already over its 40 KB target before this change.

What's left: I put the next slice on #1041 with the commit sha. It covers telling the user and the model why the tools vanished (yoagent only logs it; the data is in McpClient::exited()), restarting a dead server, and the fact that tool renames announced through list_changed are never re-checked for collisions.

Unrelated failure: anthropic_preset_tests::every_preset_id_is_priced_by_its_own_constructor fails when run on its own (claude-fable-5: owning constructor is unpriced), with or without my changes. It passes in the full suite, so its result depends on test order. I didn't touch it.
